  "query": "The wireless earbuds I'm eyeing sit at nearly five stars with thousands of happy reviews, but the hobbyist crowd keeps repeating that all true wireless buds are basically disposable: the tiny batteries fade, one side starts dropping out, and by year two you're rebuying. Those are two totally different pictures and I don't know which to believe before I spend real money. Is the battery and connection decay a physical inevitability of the format or just a few loud horror stories? I'd love the honest verdict, plus which pair holds up best if I go ahead.",
